# Set by `npx convex dev` (dev) or `npx convex deploy` (prod)
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://<your-deployment>.convex.cloud

# Where UnSplit runs, for "Split on UnSplit" (src/lib/unsplit.ts). Defaults to the live app.
# VITE_UNSPLIT_URL=http://localhost:5174

# Gmail sync (convex/gmail.ts): set on the Convex deployment, not here. 32 random bytes, base64:
#   npx convex env set GMAIL_TOKEN_KEY "$(openssl rand -base64 32)"
# The Google OAuth client also needs the redirect URI https://<deployment>.convex.site/gmail/callback.

# PostHog: product analytics, error tracking and session replay (src/lib/analytics.ts). Off when unset.
# The project API key (phc_...) from PostHog > Project settings. It is public: it ships in the app.
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...
# Events go to /ingest, which vercel.json passes on to PostHog's US cloud. For an EU project change both
# rewrites in vercel.json and the proxy in vite.config.ts to eu-assets.i.posthog.com / eu.i.posthog.com and set VITE_POSTHOG_UI_HOST=https://eu.posthog.com.
# `npm run dev` proxies /ingest the same way (vite.config.ts), so the key alone is enough locally.
# Server errors (convex/lib/posthog.ts) need the same key on the Convex deployment:
#   npx convex env set POSTHOG_KEY phc_...
